aria is a fast-moving strategy game inspired by a traditional Native American board game. Simple to learn but full of thoughtful choices, Picaria challenges players to place and move their pieces carefully as they try to create a winning line.\n\nThis app brings the classic game to life with colorful graphics, smooth touch controls, and an inviting design made especially for iPad. Players can enjoy the game while also learning about the history and cultural background of Picaria through built-in educational content.\n\nPicaria includes more than just gameplay. The app features an interactive learning section with information about the game, its origins, and how it was played. A built-in multiple-choice quiz helps students review what they have learned in a fun and engaging way. Quiz answers are scrambled each time they appear, so players must think carefully instead of memorizing the position of the correct answer.\n\nThe quiz also includes spoken questions, making the experience more accessible and lively for young learners. A score display tracks progress as a percentage, giving students immediate feedback as they work through the questions.\n\nFeatures include:\n\n• A traditional strategy game presented in a colorful digital format\n• Easy-to-use touch controls designed for iPad\n• Educational content about Picaria and its cultural background\n• Built-in multiple-choice quiz with randomized answer positions\n• Spoken quiz questions for added accessibility and engagement\n• Score tracking shown as a percentage\n• Attractive book-style learning pages\n• Helpful icons for game options, instructions, and quiz access\n• A thoughtful mix of gameplay, history, and learning\n\nPicaria is a great choice for families, classrooms, homeschool activities, and anyone interested in traditional games from world cultures. It encourages strategic thinking, careful planning, and cultural curiosity—all in one friendly app.", "minimumOsVersion": "13.2", "sellerUrl": "http://www.ventu